2c:["$","p",null,{"children":["No ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--validate"}]," flag exists. The binary takes one positional argument, the\nconfig file (plus the usual ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--help"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--version"}],"), and parses it at\nstartup, which is exactly what you want, because the check is just \"does the\nnew binary accept this file\":"]}]
